# SPDX license ids the pre-commit license gate accepts: permissive, free for unrestricted
# enterprise/commercial use, and free for redistribution. One id per line.
# See CLAUDE.md "Dependency license policy" before adding to this list.

MIT
Apache-2.0
BSD-2-Clause
BSD-3-Clause
ISC
0BSD
MS-PL
Unlicense

# Owner-approved EXCEPTION (2026-07-26), not a general license class: the Microsoft Edge WebView2 SDK
# ships under Microsoft's own free-but-proprietary license (free for commercial use and redistribution,
# not OSI). Approved solely for the studio window shell (ADR 0014). Do not reuse this id for any
# other package without a new decision.
WebView2-Microsoft-License

# Owner-approved EXCEPTIONS (2026-08-08, backlog 73), each specific to one vendor CLI, not a general
# class: the studio image bakes the Claude Code CLI, which is a proprietary vendor tool ("SEE LICENSE
# IN ..." in its npm package.json, verified 2026-08-08). These ids record ONE decision only: that
# redistributing the binary inside the studio image is an accepted vendor arrangement, reviewed with
# the vendor out of band. They say NOTHING about whether we may drive the CLI automatically -- that is
# a service-terms/commercial question this gate cannot answer, tracked under CLASSES-NOT-GATED below.
# Do not reuse these ids for any other dependency.
#
# GitHub-Copilot-Terms stays LISTED although the image no longer bakes that CLI (retired to v2, owner
# decision 2026-09-22, docs/v2.md section 1). An approved-list entry is inert without a matching line in
# licenses.allow, and removing an owner-approved exception is the owner's act, not a tidy-up.
Anthropic-Claude-Code-Terms
GitHub-Copilot-Terms

# ---- CLASSES-NOT-GATED (policy, backlog 73) --------------------------------------------------------
# The pre-commit license gate is mechanical: it can check the REDISTRIBUTION license of a dependency
# whose identity is pinned in a file it parses (NuGet packages in the project files; the npm agent CLIs
# in the Dockerfile). Some things this product ships, or is about to, are not covered by a license
# check, either because a license check is the wrong instrument or because the dependency is not yet
# pinned in a parseable place. Each is recorded here with why it is not commit-gated and how it is
# reviewed instead. When a Phase B-E dependency lands, it either becomes a real gated line above (pin
# it where the hook can parse it, record its verified license) or it is added to this list with its
# out-of-band review named. It does not land unreviewed.
#
#   Agent-CLI SERVICE TERMS (automated use). The vendor CLIs (Claude Code, Codex, Copilot) carry terms
#     about programmatic/automated use, rate, and org-key vs BYOD billing. That is a COMMERCIAL question,
#     not a license question, and a license id cannot express it, so this gate does not pretend to.
#     Reviewed out of band against each vendor's terms when a pin is promoted (ADR 0023's procedure is
#     the checkpoint); the corp-broker tier (ADR 0010) exists partly to keep automated use inside a
#     sanctioned billing arrangement.
#   Browser distribution (backlog 56, then 159). LANDED 2026-09-27 for the agent browser: Chromium's
#     headless shell, pinned through PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION in the Dockerfile (browsers.json fixes the
#     revision), is a gated line in licenses.allow now (BSD-3-Clause), beside the playwright driver
#     (Apache-2.0). Out-of-band review of terms: Chromium is an open-source build with no automated-use or
#     branding terms of its own (the Chrome brand and Google's services are not in it). Any OTHER browser
#     (a WebKit or Firefox build, a branded Chrome) starts in this block again until pinned the same way.
#   Vector / full-text extension (backlog 40). DECIDED 2026-09-19: there will not be one. Embeddings
#     are stored as BLOBs and scored in managed code, because at this product's scale (a few thousand
#     documents) a linear scan is single-digit milliseconds and a native index would be a second
#     native dependency to vendor and prove for no gain. sqlite-vec (Apache-2.0, verified) stays the
#     upgrade path; if it is ever adopted it becomes a gated line above.
#   Embedding / OCR model weights (backlog 40 and later). Model weights are DATA, not a library, and
#     carry their own model licenses (often non-OSI, with field-of-use limits) that an SPDX id does not
#     capture. Reviewed out of band per model before it ships; recorded here, never silently bundled.
#     DECIDED 2026-09-19 for the wiki embedder: all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (Apache-2.0, verified against the
#     Hugging Face model metadata), baked into the image because the container runs offline. Baking it
#     makes it a redistribution question, so it does NOT stay in this block: pin the model id and its
#     revision as Dockerfile ARGs the way CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION is pinned, and add the gated line above
#     when the code lands. LANDED 2026-09-21: it is a gated line in licenses.allow now, pinned in the
#     Dockerfile by revision and per-file SHA-256, and EmbeddingModelPinTests reads those lines. Any
#     OTHER model (a second embedder, OCR) starts in this block again until it is pinned the same way.
#   Inno Setup 6 (setup/webinstall). A BUILD TOOL, not a linked library, so it is pinned nowhere the
#     hook can parse; its setup stub does ride inside the generated FravashiWebSetup.exe. License
#     verified 2026-08-25 against jrsoftware/issrc license.txt: zlib-style, "use this software for any
#     purpose, including commercial applications", redistribution permitted with notices retained
#     (the generated stub retains them by default).
#     RETIRED 2026-10-13 (backlog 296, decided 2026-10-11): replaced by a bootstrapper of our own.
#     FravashiSetup.exe is now our own WinForms bootstrapper (src/Fravashi.WebSetup), built with
#     nothing but the .NET SDK. This note stays as history.
